201 C.F.R. § 655.88 of the FAR provides that "systems security" must be provided. System security, as defined in the FAR, is the safeguarding of unclassified information systems that maintain, process, store, or transmit Federal contractor information from unauthorized use, disclosure, modification, disruption, or destruction. The FAR makes no distinction between cyber and traditional security, but does provide that each contractor must have a plan that "provides for the identification and assessment of security controls, and the establishment of a security policy, including principles for system security." For purposes of this question, we are interested in the cyber security requirements that the FAR imposes on Federal contractors.
The FAR, at § 252.204-7012, requires that each covered contractor identify and assess risks to the security of unclassified information systems. This includes risks to personal information. The Contractor shall provide appropriate safeguards to control risks identified in the assessment. The Contractor is also required to design and document its system security plan. In addition, the Contractor shall establish and implement a security plan as required by the Federal Security Policy Standards for the protection of unclassified information. Each system security plan shall provide that:
(i) Each information system used to maintain, process, store, or transmit Federal contractor information will be protected by an appropriate level of security based on a risk assessment;
(ii) Security controls will be implemented, tested, and evaluated to ensure compliance with system security plan requirements;
(iii) The procedures to be followed in the event of an information system security incident;
(iv) A plan to protect against the unauthorized access, use, disclosure, disruption, modification, or destruction of information system resources and the integrity, confidentiality, and availability of information;
(v) A plan for emergency operations that are coordinated with the Contracting Officer to restore the availability and integrity of information systems, and access to information;
(vi) A plan to ensure the continuity of services to accomplish essential agency functions in the event of an information system interruption;
(vii) A plan to identify and to recover information systems that are critical to agency operations, including documentation of the criteria used to determine the criticality of information systems, and a list of those information systems;
(viii) A plan to identify and to assess the risks associated with the use of external information systems;
(ix) A plan for the documentation, testing, and evaluation of security controls for information systems;
(x) A plan for the documentation, testing, and evaluation of security controls for the continuity of operations for mission critical information systems;
(xi) A plan for contingency operations to provide for the continued operations of essential agency functions;
(xii) A plan to detect, document, and report information system security incidents;
(xiii) A plan to ensure adequate privacy protections of personal information collected, maintained, used, and disseminated in accordance with the agency's Privacy Act System of Records Notice (SORN);
(xiv) A plan to ensure proper disposal of sensitive and other information in accordance with the agency's records management requirements and privacy requirements;
(xv) A plan to ensure compliance with applicable information sharing guidelines;
(xvi) A plan to provide security training for personnel;
(xvii) A plan to provide information concerning information system security to personnel;
(xviii) A plan to provide information concerning information system security to users of information systems;
(xix) A plan to provide information concerning information system security to individuals;
(xx) A plan for a system security management program that is commensurate with the level of risk and complexity of information systems;
(xxi) A plan to ensure that security controls for information systems are implemented and maintained;
(xxii) A plan to ensure that security controls are reviewed for continued adequacy;
(xxiii) A plan to ensure that security controls are monitored and tested;
(xxiv) A plan to ensure that security controls are compliant with applicable Federal laws and regulations; and
